.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead label remove" 1  "bead label remove " 
.SH NAME
bead label remove \- Remove a label from an issue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead label remove\fR <\fB\-\-label\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a label from an issue (idempotent).
.PP
Removes the specified label from the issue. If the label does not exist,
the command succeeds without making changes.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead label remove bead\-123abc456789def \-\-label bug
  bead label remove ID \-\-label urgent
.PP
IDEMPOTENCY:
  Removing a non\-existent label succeeds without error.
  This makes label management safe and declarative.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR=\fILABEL\fR
Label to remove
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
